 "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1b/08/17/91/pashupati.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2020-02-28", "published_at_date": "2020-02-28"}, {"review_id": 748072817, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r748072817-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Interesting dirt hindhu temple", "text": "It is highly recommended and visited by almost 100% of extranal tourist and internal. This is the largest hindhu temple by value. The pashupatinath is the lord shiva temple that believes, anyone visit to the temple and do a worship of Lord shive then it keeps the faith the Lord will bless anything you ask for. Nearly one thousand old temple was founded at the time a cow pouring her milk to a bare hole 🕳. As the information found this is the oldest crematorium of Nepal 🇳🇵. The worship in the temple happened twice a day a early morning and in the evening after sunset 🌇. The belief of burning dead body is a big faith that the Lord will take the  dead soul go to the heaven and God himself look after that dead person. There are many different occasions and worship all dedicate to Lord shiva. The shivarAtri (शिवरात्री) is a huge festival in pashupati. It is believed the shivarAtri is the birthday of Lord shiva as well some say it is Lord's marriage day. But as the religion says that shiva has no parents so nobody know how shiva had born. \nEvery evening's worship is a best thing to see but the dirty pashupati by the visitors is making ugly pashupati. So the community should think about this. As seen it clearly at the moment pashupati is a best way of the business of pashupati development communities. It just said because there is not such thought has been put about the tourist facilities and the cleaning of the area. Another important is 100% monkeys in pashupati have HIV so visitors should aware with that. You all have recommendation for touring of pashupatinath Temple but the concert is the PDC have to think about the clean of the place and provide a authentic atmosphere of what does pashupatinath means. Because of the uncleanness I couldn't rate a 5* for this site. \nДякую Непал 🇳🇵 🙏 Nepal 🇳🇵 ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2020-02-29"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4AC6748B468CC4F676C2A37175D332EF", "name": "Андрей харел", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/travelthecontinent", "username": "travelthecontinent", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/73/2c/65/travelforleisureworl.jpg", "contribution_count": 179, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1b/07/b1/28/mg-8548-largejpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1b/07/b1/29/img-20191231-wa0024-largejpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1b/07/b1/2a/mg-8608-largejpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2020-02-28", "published_at_date": "2020-02-28"}, {"review_id": 747957796, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r747957796-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Remarkable Hindu Temple", "text": "I visited during a Hindu festival and it was really a significant cultural site to behold. The temple is beautiful with many vibrant colors and very nice people.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2020-02-29"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "09F3AA44A4DD3B717666A62AAB41C482", "name": "SF Guy", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/CaliGuy01", "username": "CaliGuy01", "avatar": "https://d